      "content": "Critics argue that these agreements can disproportionately favor large, established economies that possess greater resources and lobbying power. Smaller nations may struggle to compete with the massive production scale and economies of scale enjoyed by global giants. Furthermore, some local industries can be devastated by cheap imports allowed under these treaties, leading to job losses and domestic economic strain. This uneven playing field raises concerns about equitable development and sovereignty.",
